 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \log N)$ for sorting, plus $O(M \cdot R^2)$ for rasterization, where $N$ is the total number of Gaussians, $M$ is the number of visible Gaussians, and $R$ is the average radius (capped at 15).
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ to store Gaussian attributes and intermediate arrays.
-*   **Performance:** Suitable for low-resolution outputs or small scenes due to CPU-bound processing. Not suitable for real-time rendering or high-resolution video generation without significant optimization [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Simple implementation, easy to debug, no GPU dependency.
-*   **Limitations:** Slow for large scenes, no support for differentiable rendering, limited by CPU cache and memory bandwidth.
